  "text": "proprium.commemoratio-omnium-fidelium-defunctorum-missa-ii-evangelium",
  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Commemoration of All the Faithful Departed — Mass II” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": {
      "translation": "At that time, Jesus said to the multitude of the Jews, All that the Father gives to Me shall come to Me, and him who comes to Me I will not cast out. For I have come down from heaven, not to do My own will, but the will of Him Who sent Me. Now this is the will of Him Who sent Me, the Father, that I should lose nothing of what He has given Me, but that I should raise it up on the last day. For this is the will of My Father Who sent Me, that whoever beholds the Son, and believes in Him, shall have everlasting life, and I will raise him up on the last day."
    }
  },
